{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have portable snapshots wired. The agent writes a full workspace. You do\nnot want every file in durable storage."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"policy"},{"type":"text","value":" when you create the snapshots object. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"include"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"exclude"},{"type":"text","value":"\nare functions. They decide which workspace paths the capture stores. The same\npolicy runs on automatic save, named save, and restore."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page assumes you already created a snapshots object. If you have not, start\nwith "},{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-configure","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep Files After Reload"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"default-exclusions-stay-unless-you-pass-exclude","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default exclusions stay unless you pass exclude"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you pass only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"include"},{"type":"text","value":" or only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redact"},{"type":"text","value":", the default exclusions stay\nin place. Capture still skips "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".git"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node_modules"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"exclude"},{"type":"text","value":", that function replaces the default exclusions.\nCopy "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()"},{"type":"text","value":" first. Then keep those rules and add\nyours."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string) {\n    return path === 'src' || path.startsWith('src/')\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The projection marker for this workspace stays protected. A custom policy\ncannot capture or restore that marker."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pass-the-policy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the policy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"policy"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memorySandboxSnapshots"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSandboxSnapshots"},{"type":"text","value":". Use that\nsame object in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport {\n  defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  InMemorySandboxInstanceStore,\n  memorySandboxSnapshots,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nconst instances = new InMemorySandboxInstanceStore()\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'app-builder',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'none' } }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread' },\n})\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst snapshots = await memorySandboxSnapshots({\n  sandbox,\n  instances,\n  policy: {\n    ...defaults,\n    include(path: string) {\n      return path === 'src' || path.startsWith('src/')\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nconst result = chat({\n  threadId: 'app-thread',\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Create a landing page.' }],\n  middleware: [\n    withPersistence(snapshots.persistence),\n    withSandbox(sandbox, { instances, snapshots }),\n  ],\n})\n\nvoid result","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snapshots.save"},{"type":"text","value":" has no file list. Change the file set by changing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"policy"},{"type":"text","value":" on\nthe snapshots object."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-include-and-exclude-run","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How include and exclude run"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each path is a workspace-relative string such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/app.ts"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"kind"},{"type":"text","value":" is\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dir"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The projection marker is skipped."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"exclude(path, kind)"},{"type":"text","value":" returns true, the path is skipped. For a\ndirectory, the whole tree under it is skipped."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a file, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"include(path, 'file')"},{"type":"text","value":" must return true. If you omit\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"include"},{"type":"text","value":", every file that is not excluded is stored."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capture then walks parent directories so a nested file can still match."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"exclude"},{"type":"text","value":" wins. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"include: () => true"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot keep a path that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"exclude"},{"type":"text","value":"\nrejects."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capture does not read a file that the policy skips."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keep-one-file","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep one file"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return true only for that path. Capture still walks parent directories."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string) {\n    return path === 'src/app.ts'\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keep-a-few-files","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep a few files"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\nconst keep = new Set(['package.json', 'src/app.ts', 'src/index.ts'])\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string) {\n    return keep.has(path)\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keep-one-folder","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep one folder"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string) {\n    return path === 'src' || path.startsWith('src/')\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keep-files-by-suffix","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep files by suffix"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Allow directories so the walk can reach nested files. Then match the suffix."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string, kind: 'file' | 'dir') {\n    return kind === 'dir' || path.endsWith('.ts')\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"skip-one-extra-folder","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skip one extra folder"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep the default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"exclude"},{"type":"text","value":". Then add your folder."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  exclude(path: string, kind: 'file' | 'dir') {\n    if (defaults.exclude?.(path, kind)) return true\n    return path === 'dist' || path.startsWith('dist/')\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To skip a folder name at every depth, match a path segment:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  exclude(path: string, kind: 'file' | 'dir') {\n    if (defaults.exclude?.(path, kind)) return true\n    return path.split('/').includes('dist')\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-the-policy-does-not-filter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What the policy does not filter"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The file policy applies to workspace files and empty directories only."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The checkpoint still stores the full conversation for the thread."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The checkpoint still copies every generated artifact for the thread."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-safety","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What a Snapshot Stores"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for secrets, default\nexclusions, and restore safety."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"restore","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Restore"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Restore uses the same policy. Files that the policy does not include stay on\nthe destination disk. Restore does not delete those files."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic restore still writes the latest checkpoint into a new private\nsandbox. It does not write into a live resumed sandbox."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"default-exclusions-stay-unless-you-pass-exclude","text":"Default exclusions stay unless you pass exclude","level":2},{"id":"pass-the-policy","text":"Pass the policy","level":2},{"id":"how-include-and-exclude-run","text":"How include and exclude run","level":2},{"id":"keep-one-file","text":"Keep one file","level":2},{"id":"keep-a-few-files","text":"Keep a few files","level":2},{"id":"keep-one-folder","text":"Keep one folder","level":2},{"id":"keep-files-by-suffix","text":"Keep files by suffix","level":2},{"id":"skip-one-extra-folder","text":"Skip one extra folder","level":2},{"id":"what-the-policy-does-not-filter","text":"What the policy does not filter","level":2},{"id":"restore","text":"Restore","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou have portable snapshots wired. The agent writes a full workspace. You do\nnot want every file in durable storage.\n\nPass a `policy` when you create the snapshots object. `include` and `exclude`\nare functions. They decide which workspace paths the capture stores. The same\npolicy runs on automatic save, named save, and restore.\n\nThis page assumes you already created a snapshots object. If you have not, start\nwith [Keep Files After Reload](./portable-snapshots-configure).\n\n## Default exclusions stay unless you pass exclude\n\nIf you pass only `include` or only `redact`, the default exclusions stay\nin place. Capture still skips `.env`, `.git`, and `node_modules`.\n\nIf you pass `exclude`, that function replaces the default exclusions.\nCopy `defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()` first. Then keep those rules and add\nyours.\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string) {\n    return path === 'src' || path.startsWith('src/')\n  },\n}\n```\n\nThe projection marker for this workspace stays protected. A custom policy\ncannot capture or restore that marker.\n\n## Pass the policy\n\nPass `policy` to `memorySandboxSnapshots` or `createSandboxSnapshots`. Use that\nsame object in `withSandbox`.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport {\n  defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  InMemorySandboxInstanceStore,\n  memorySandboxSnapshots,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nconst instances = new InMemorySandboxInstanceStore()\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'app-builder',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'none' } }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread' },\n})\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst snapshots = await memorySandboxSnapshots({\n  sandbox,\n  instances,\n  policy: {\n    ...defaults,\n    include(path: string) {\n      return path === 'src' || path.startsWith('src/')\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nconst result = chat({\n  threadId: 'app-thread',\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Create a landing page.' }],\n  middleware: [\n    withPersistence(snapshots.persistence),\n    withSandbox(sandbox, { instances, snapshots }),\n  ],\n})\n\nvoid result\n```\n\n`snapshots.save` has no file list. Change the file set by changing `policy` on\nthe snapshots object.\n\n## How include and exclude run\n\nEach path is a workspace-relative string such as `src/app.ts`. `kind` is\n`file` or `dir`.\n\n1. The projection marker is skipped.\n2. If `exclude(path, kind)` returns true, the path is skipped. For a\n   directory, the whole tree under it is skipped.\n3. For a file, `include(path, 'file')` must return true. If you omit\n   `include`, every file that is not excluded is stored.\n4. Capture then walks parent directories so a nested file can still match.\n\n`exclude` wins. `include: () => true` cannot keep a path that `exclude`\nrejects.\n\nCapture does not read a file that the policy skips.\n\n## Keep one file\n\nReturn true only for that path. Capture still walks parent directories.\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string) {\n    return path === 'src/app.ts'\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Keep a few files\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\nconst keep = new Set(['package.json', 'src/app.ts', 'src/index.ts'])\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string) {\n    return keep.has(path)\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Keep one folder\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string) {\n    return path === 'src' || path.startsWith('src/')\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Keep files by suffix\n\nAllow directories so the walk can reach nested files. Then match the suffix.\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string, kind: 'file' | 'dir') {\n    return kind === 'dir' || path.endsWith('.ts')\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Skip one extra folder\n\nKeep the default `exclude`. Then add your folder.\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  exclude(path: string, kind: 'file' | 'dir') {\n    if (defaults.exclude?.(path, kind)) return true\n    return path === 'dist' || path.startsWith('dist/')\n  },\n}\n```\n\nTo skip a folder name at every depth, match a path segment:\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  exclude(path: string, kind: 'file' | 'dir') {\n    if (defaults.exclude?.(path, kind)) return true\n    return path.split('/').includes('dist')\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## What the policy does not filter\n\nThe file policy applies to workspace files and empty directories only.\n\n- The checkpoint still stores the full conversation for the thread.\n- The checkpoint still copies every generated artifact for the thread.\n\nSee [What a Snapshot Stores](./portable-snapshots-safety) for secrets, default\nexclusions, and restore safety.\n\n## Restore\n\nRestore uses the same policy. Files that the policy does not include stay on\nthe destination disk. Restore does not delete those files.\n\nAutomatic restore still writes the latest checkpoint into a new private\nsandbox. It does not write into a live resumed sandbox.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Pick Which Files to Keep\nid: portable-snapshots-files\norder: 15\ndescription: \"Pass include and exclude functions so a portable snapshot stores only the files you choose, including a single file.\"\n---\n\nYou have portable snapshots wired. The agent writes a full workspace. You do\nnot want every file in durable storage.\n\nPass a `policy` when you create the snapshots object. `include` and `exclude`\nare functions. They decide which workspace paths the capture stores. The same\npolicy runs on automatic save, named save, and restore.\n\nThis page assumes you already created a snapshots object. If you have not, start\nwith [Keep Files After Reload](./portable-snapshots-configure).\n\n## Default exclusions stay unless you pass exclude\n\nIf you pass only `include` or only `redact`, the default exclusions stay\nin place. Capture still skips `.env`, `.git`, and `node_modules`.\n\nIf you pass `exclude`, that function replaces the default exclusions.\nCopy `defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()` first. Then keep those rules and add\nyours.\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string) {\n    return path === 'src' || path.startsWith('src/')\n  },\n}\n```\n\nThe projection marker for this workspace stays protected. A custom policy\ncannot capture or restore that marker.\n\n## Pass the policy\n\nPass `policy` to `memorySandboxSnapshots` or `createSandboxSnapshots`. Use that\nsame object in `withSandbox`.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport {\n  defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  InMemorySandboxInstanceStore,\n  memorySandboxSnapshots,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nconst instances = new InMemorySandboxInstanceStore()\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'app-builder',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'none' } }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread' },\n})\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst snapshots = await memorySandboxSnapshots({\n  sandbox,\n  instances,\n  policy: {\n    ...defaults,\n    include(path: string) {\n      return path === 'src' || path.startsWith('src/')\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nconst result = chat({\n  threadId: 'app-thread',\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Create a landing page.' }],\n  middleware: [\n    withPersistence(snapshots.persistence),\n    withSandbox(sandbox, { instances, snapshots }),\n  ],\n})\n\nvoid result\n```\n\n`snapshots.save` has no file list. Change the file set by changing `policy` on\nthe snapshots object.\n\n## How include and exclude run\n\nEach path is a workspace-relative string such as `src/app.ts`. `kind` is\n`file` or `dir`.\n\n1. The projection marker is skipped.\n2. If `exclude(path, kind)` returns true, the path is skipped. For a\n   directory, the whole tree under it is skipped.\n3. For a file, `include(path, 'file')` must return true. If you omit\n   `include`, every file that is not excluded is stored.\n4. Capture then walks parent directories so a nested file can still match.\n\n`exclude` wins. `include: () => true` cannot keep a path that `exclude`\nrejects.\n\nCapture does not read a file that the policy skips.\n\n## Keep one file\n\nReturn true only for that path. Capture still walks parent directories.\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string) {\n    return path === 'src/app.ts'\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Keep a few files\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\nconst keep = new Set(['package.json', 'src/app.ts', 'src/index.ts'])\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string) {\n    return keep.has(path)\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Keep one folder\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string) {\n    return path === 'src' || path.startsWith('src/')\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Keep files by suffix\n\nAllow directories so the walk can reach nested files. Then match the suffix.\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  include(path: string, kind: 'file' | 'dir') {\n    return kind === 'dir' || path.endsWith('.ts')\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Skip one extra folder\n\nKeep the default `exclude`. Then add your folder.\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  exclude(path: string, kind: 'file' | 'dir') {\n    if (defaults.exclude?.(path, kind)) return true\n    return path === 'dist' || path.startsWith('dist/')\n  },\n}\n```\n\nTo skip a folder name at every depth, match a path segment:\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst defaults = defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaults,\n  exclude(path: string, kind: 'file' | 'dir') {\n    if (defaults.exclude?.(path, kind)) return true\n    return path.split('/').includes('dist')\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## What the policy does not filter\n\nThe file policy applies to workspace files and empty directories only.\n\n- The checkpoint still stores the full conversation for the thread.\n- The checkpoint still copies every generated artifact for the thread.\n\nSee [What a Snapshot Stores](./portable-snapshots-safety) for secrets, default\nexclusions, and restore safety.\n\n## Restore\n\nRestore uses the same policy. Files that the policy does not include stay on\nthe destination disk. Restore does not delete those files.\n\nAutomatic restore still writes the latest checkpoint into a new private\nsandbox. It does not write into a live resumed sandbox.\n"}
